On Tue, Nov 09, 2010 at 09:30:53PM -0500, Luke Bergen wrote:
>    Here's a fun game. I may or may not have already done something similar
>    (my memory is shite), so if I have, just ignore me, otherwise...
>    1) Take your english name and insert as many spaces/.'s as it takes to
>    make everything in it a valid lojban word, whether it parses or not. If
>    it's not anything at all like a lojban word, try mixing in your middle
>    name/initial.
>    2) Post the results.
>    3) ???
>    4) Profit
>    For example.
>    Luke Bergen -> lu ke bergen -> [quote][start-grouping]north grammar
>    mu'o mi'e cribe
> 

My name has a 'la' in it, which is forbidden outside of dotside,
which itself is not official yet.  Applying the naive algorithm, I
get some invalid combinations: npo and ost:

Alan Post => .a.la.npost

So I'll need to break those up by adding vowels to get at the valid
'pos' rafsi.  Given my name's fondness for the letter 'a', I'll use
that:

.a la na pos ta

inclusive-or name-sumti-tag negate ponse-rafsi(posses) that

-Alan
